WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.600
Phase 0 wanted ninety minutes on the server.

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.800
Build a toolchain on production, and measure.

3
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.300
An experiment leaves things behind.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:17.100
Every one of them becomes an assumption.

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.200
And a stopwatch in the box measures the box.

6
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.000
The user waits through the network too.

7
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.300
Most of the questions were not about hardware.

8
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.100
Weights and flags. Both answerable here.

9
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.400
So it ran on this laptop instead.

10
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.200
Three points between the two candidates.

11
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.700
And the small one invented a price.

12
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.000
On the page that publishes none.

13
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.300
The cache question took one flag.

14
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.800
Same score. Most of a gigabyte back.

15
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.300
Two criteria closed in an afternoon.

16
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.200
They had been blocked on a terminal.
